1) File Deduplication: Before a file starts its upload sequence, send the local calculated hash checksum to the server. 
If that specific signature matches an existing backend block, link the client's metadata directly to the current storage address without writing duplicate raw chunks.

2) Database Sharding: Scale out metadata storage by horizontally partitioning records across database nodes 
using owner_id as the primary shard key to ensure all user directories cluster closely together
